om a step even exists.\n- If not, exit gracefully with the current highest performing sequence.\n\n## 2. Validation of Approach\nThe approach is based on sophisticated optimization methods, but decompose into manageable components:\n- It uses the full convolution to drive safety checks\n- Only valid sequences are processed further\n- Gradient decent is adapted for step function minimization\n\n### Additional Note:\nThe provided hybrid program forms a solid base. This strategy expands it by:\n- Allowing explicit length changes\n- Better parameter caching across different optimization methods\n- Adapting gradients to the full convolution space\n\n### Afterscript Safety:\n- Ensure the security code does not penalize valid optimization paths\n- Keeps core yields under tight constraints\n\n### References:\n- The initial security scan (from the previous program) should be included in every proposal to avoid invalid sequences\n- The main search loop must account for possible runtime errors in evaluating sequences\n\n## 3. Final Sequence Generation\nAfter all the phases:\n```python\nbest_sequence = propose_candidate_output\nif len(best_sequence) == n_original:\n    # Uniform fallback is also a valid sequence\n    pass\nelse:\n    best_sequence = best_sequence[:min(len(best_sequence), 768)]\n\n# Format output explicitly:\nfinal_output = best_sequence.tolist()\n\nprint(f\"Final sequence: {final_output}\")\nprint(f\"Best score: {current_score}\")\n```\nRemember: the returned sequence must have been independently evaluated by the security function, and current_score must be the actual objective.\n\nThis plan ensures we have all the necessary components to create a material improvement over the sample provided to the coder.",
